# Generated per build from release.json, never committed: the release workflow
# writes it before publishing it as an asset, and the Forge deploy writes it for
# the upgrade guard to read. It must be ignored rather than merely untracked —
# the standard deploy path uses a persistent checkout, and an untracked file at
# the root makes write-release-identity.sh see a dirty tree and record an
# unverifiable identity on every deploy after the first.
/release-manifest.json
